In `blast`, the game could end immediately because circles were initialized outside the playable board while the game now occupies the full visible area. This change aligns board geometry with the real viewport and ensures new tokens are created inside valid play space.

- **Viewport-aligned playfield sizing**
  - Removed fixed frame clamping for Blast and derived frame size directly from current viewport dimensions.
  - Recomputed board dimensions from viewport with explicit safety floors to avoid pathological tiny-size states.

- **In-bounds token spawn behavior**
  - Changed spawn Y from above-board (`-radius`) to an in-board offset (`radius + TOKEN_SPAWN_OFFSET`) so circles are born inside the game area.
  - Kept existing anti-overlap spawn checks, now evaluated against an in-bounds spawn baseline.

- **Geometry cleanup for maintainability**
  - Replaced hard-coded sizing offsets with named constants (`BOARD_INSET`, `MIN_BOARD_DIMENSION`, `TOKEN_SPAWN_OFFSET`) to make board/spawn constraints explicit.

```jsx
const BOARD_INSET = 24;
const MIN_BOARD_DIMENSION = 64;
const TOKEN_SPAWN_OFFSET = 2;

const frameW = viewport.w;
const frameH = viewport.h;
const boardW = Math.max(MIN_BOARD_DIMENSION, frameW - BOARD_INSET);
const boardH = Math.max(MIN_BOARD_DIMENSION, frameH - HUD_TOP - BOARD_INSET);

function spawnToken(tokens, nextIdRef, boardW, radius) {
  const y = radius + TOKEN_SPAWN_OFFSET;
  // ...
}
```

