On mobile, `100vh` includes browser chrome (address bar), making `#screen-turn` taller than the actual visible viewport — the action buttons (Trouvé / Passer / Erreur) were pushed below the fold. The word card also couldn't shrink properly, preventing `fitWordCard()` from using full available width.

## Changes

- **`#screen-turn`**: Replace `min-height: 100vh` with `height: 100dvh` (with `100vh` fallback), add `overflow: hidden` and `box-sizing: border-box` — container now fits exactly the visible viewport
- **`.word-card`**: Add `min-height: 0` — allows the flex child to shrink below content size so the JS binary-search font-sizer can exploit the full card width
- **Landscape media query**: Consistent update from `min-height: 100svh` → `height: 100dvh`

```css
#screen-turn {
  height: 100vh;
  height: 100dvh;   /* dynamic: excludes browser chrome */
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

.word-card {
  flex: 1;
  min-height: 0;    /* allows shrink in flex column */
}
```

