Applies a batch of code-review fixes spanning test correctness, storage security hardening, and an API error constructor bug.

## Changes

### `src/App.test.tsx`
- Replace empty `await waitFor(() => {})` with `await Promise.resolve()` — removes fragile implicit-timeout dependency
- Remove module-scoped `seededAuthUser`; seed helpers now call `mockGetCurrentUser.mockResolvedValue()` directly, making mock coupling explicit
- Extract `ROUTE_NAVIGATION_TIMEOUT_MS = 20_000` constant; replaces all 15 magic-number occurrences

### `src/hooks/useAuth.test.ts`
- Replace all plaintext `localStorage.setItem("auth_user", JSON.stringify(...))` with `await authStorage.setUser()` so tests exercise the real encryption layer
- Update `localStorage.getItem` assertions to `await expect(authStorage.getUser()).resolves.toEqual(...)`
- Add `waitFor` around the intermediate bootstrap user-state check — encrypted storage is async; the synchronous `getUserSnapshot()` returns `null` for encrypted envelopes

### `src/pages/Login.test.tsx`
- Replace Node.js-only `Buffer.from` with `Uint8Array.from(new TextEncoder().encode(value)).buffer` — the `Uint8Array.from` wrapper is required for jsdom cross-realm `instanceof ArrayBuffer` compatibility
- Clarify `mockRejectedValue` (not `Once`) comment

### `src/services/employeeApi.ts`
- Fix `ApiError` constructor arg order in BWR export and BWR status update: third argument was `response` (the `Response` object) instead of `normalizeApiErrorErrors(error.errors) ?? undefined`

### `src/services/storage.ts`
- Raise PBKDF2 iteration count from `5_000` → `600_000` (OWASP minimum for PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256)
- Add `try/catch` around `JSON.parse` in `decryptPersistedAuthUser` — malformed envelopes now return `null` cleanly instead of throwing
- Extract `clearInvalidStoredUser()` and `handleStoredUserError()` private helpers to eliminate duplicated remove-and-return-null patterns in `getUserSnapshot` / `getUser`
- Improve CSRF-missing `console.warn` message to state the actual root cause

